### What are you really trying to do?

Using uuid() in query handlers (or validate update) can cause subsequent calls to uuid() in the workflow code to produce non-deterministic values.

eg: 
```


export async function example(name: string): Promise<string> {
  let confirmed = false;

  setHandler(getStatusQuery, () => {
    const s = uuid4(); //if this is called first 
    return s;
  });

  setHandler(confirm, () => {
    confirmed = true;
  });

  await condition(() => confirmed);

  const child_id = uuid4(); //this value will be different during replay

  await executeChild(example_child, {
    workflowId: child_id,
    args: ['Child Workflow'],
  });
  return "done";
}


```


